"""Render corrected DITL audit/LaTeX blocks from recalculated JSON, preserving other studies."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,csv,re
from validate_corrected_ditl import ROOT,OUT,SCENARIOS,dump
S={s:json.loads((OUT/(s+'_summary.json')).read_text()) for s in SCENARIOS}
from validate_corrected_ditl import selected
for scenario,summary in S.items():
 if summary['run_id']!=selected(scenario,verify=False)['run_id']:raise ValueError('Summary identity differs from authoritative registry')
y=S['leop_1yr'];a=S['leop_24h'];b=S['no_leop_24h']
texdir=ROOT/'sections/corrected_ditl';texdir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
def n(v):return f'{v:,.3f}'.rstrip('0').rstrip('.') if isinstance(v,float) else f'{v:,}' if isinstance(v,int) else str(v)
def tx(s):return str(s).replace('_',r'\_').replace('%',r'\%').replace('&',r'\&')
def table(caption,label,headers,rows):
 cols='X'+'r'*(len(headers)-1)
 return '\\begin{table}[H]\\centering\\small\n\\caption{'+caption+'}\\label{'+label+'}\n\\begin{tabularx}{\\linewidth}{@{}'+cols+'@{}}\\toprule\n'+' & '.join(headers)+r'\\\midrule'+'\n'+'\n'.join(' & '.join(map(str,row))+r'\\' for row in rows)+'\n\\bottomrule\\end{tabularx}\\end{table}\n'
def fig(name,cap,label):return '\\begin{figure}[H]\\centering\\includegraphics[width=\\linewidth]{evidence/science-ditl/figures/corrected_20261109_'+name+'.png}\n\\caption{'+cap+'}\\label{'+label+'}\\end{figure}\n'
def write(name,s):(texdir/(name+'.tex')).write_text('% Generated corrected-evidence block; see registry and audit.\n'+s)
def metric(s,k):return s.get(k,0)
q=next(q for q in y['queues'] if q['case'].endswith('EMSC_3'))
rows=[('Recorded timestamp span (s)','duration_s'),('Sun Pointing (s)','mode:SUN_POINTING'),('Detection (s)','mode:DETECTION'),('Relay (s)','mode:RELAY'),('Slewing (s)','mode:SLEWING'),('Safe (s)','mode:SAFE'),('Geographic SAA (s)','saa_s'),('Acquisition gate (s)','acquisition_gate_s'),('Minimum recorded battery (Wh)','battery_min_wh'),('Recorded solar integral (Wh)','generated_wh'),('Recorded load integral (Wh)','consumed_wh'),('Native generation (source MB)','generated_source_mb'),('Native transfer (source MB)','transferred_source_mb')]
def val(s,k):return s['mode_seconds'].get(k[5:],0) if k.startswith('mode:') else s[k]
main=r'''\subsection{Day-in-the-Life Operations}\label{sec:sim-leop}
The corrected exports under \path{evidence/new-science-ditl/} replace the previously ingested incorrect/incomplete Science/DITL evidence. The old raw files, analyses and PDFs remain archived and must not support current numerical conclusions. The registry selects one source identity per scenario; no rows are pooled across runs. All three exports reach their named timestamp horizons: two 24-hour cases and one 365-day case. Absolute contact and SAA timestamps consistently identify 1 March 2000 UTC, not the approved 2029 analysis epoch.

The files contain no producing commit or runtime manifest. RAAN, mass, battery capacity, integrator, selected hardware and elevation mask therefore remain unverified. The two day cases have matching recorded orbital positions and contact windows to numerical precision, but complete configuration equivalence is not established. Their comparison is a sensitivity study, not a controlled causal test of LEOP alone.

The following telemetry integrals hold each recorded state over $[t_i,t_{i+1})$, exclude terminal-row duration, and sum to the recorded horizon. These exports lack explicit interval-end fields. Transition-log mode durations and slew-event durations are reported separately in Appendix~\ref{app:ditl-detail}; disagreements are not silently removed. Battery percentages elsewhere use 25 Wh only as an identified planning normalization, not a recovered capacity.
'''
main+=table('Corrected telemetry accounting; left-held interval interpretation, historical epoch','tab:annual-ditl',['Metric','LEOP 24 h','No-LEOP 24 h','LEOP 365 d'],[[title]+[n(val(s,k)) for s in [a,b,y]] for title,k in rows])
main+=fig('day_occupancy_battery','Corrected day-run mode occupancy and battery normalized to the 25 Wh planning reference. Same time span does not establish identical runtime configuration.','fig:annual-mode-exposure')
main+=f"Both day runs record {n(a['saa_s'])} s geographic SAA dwell and {n(a['acquisition_gate_s'])} s acquisition gate. Removing startup does not increase this gate total in the supplied pair. LEOP includes one {n(a['event_checks']['detumble_events']['sum_duration_s'])} s detumble event; this is not Monte Carlo reliability. For the annual trace, acquisition/SAA is {100*y['acquisition_gate_s']/y['saa_s']:.3f}\\%, with numerator {n(y['acquisition_gate_s'])} s and denominator {n(y['saa_s'])} s. Neither fraction is calibrated current-FPDU science duty.\n"
main+=r'''
Geographic SAA passages, sampled cell visits, gated exposure, model expected counts, accepted detector events and received science products are distinct. The legacy response does not qualify the six-scintillator FPDU. No MMSC/MSC/EMSC success percentage follows from these operational records.
\subsection{Ground Station and Data Return}\label{sec:sim-coverage}
'''
c=y['contacts'];main+=f"The corrected annual contact log contains {c['count']} intervals totaling {n(c['duration_s'])} s. Mean daily contact is {n(c['daily_mean_s'])} s and minimum daily contact {n(c['daily_min_s'])} s; the longest intercontact gap is {n(c['max_gap_s'])} s. The source mask is unknown and is not applied a second time. Visibility alone corresponds to {n(c['visibility_capacity_bytes'])} bytes at 19.2 kbps. Intersecting these contacts with telemetry-labelled Relay yields {n(c['relay_overlap_s'])} s, or {n(c['relay_capacity_bytes'])} ideal bytes. Transition-log Relay instead gives {n(y['event_mode_relay_capacity_bytes'])} bytes; the timing-definition sensitivity remains explicit.\n\n"
main+=f"Native annual transfer credit is {y['transferred_source_mb']:.9f} source-labelled MB, separate from hypothetical v3 delivery. Source MB scaling and received-packet integrity are not demonstrated by the label. The v3 preferred EMSC workload generates {n(q['generated_bytes'])} bytes with peak modeled queue {n(q['peak_required_bytes'])} bytes and final backlog {n(q['remaining_bytes'])} bytes. It uses corrected, time-aligned sampled gates and Relay visibility at the full ideal 2400 bytes/s; it is not emitted v3 telemetry. Appendix~\\ref{{app:science-data-budget}} gives tier and outage sensitivity.\n"
main+=r'''The preliminary communications assessment uses the full idealized 19.2 kbps gross transfer opportunity during eligible ground-station relay windows. No arbitrary link derating is imposed at MCR. Detailed RF link-budget closure, protocol overhead, packet losses, retransmissions, and achievable net payload throughput shall be assessed at PDR.
'''
write('operations',main)
# Detailed annual evidence, retaining independent detumble appendix outside this generated block.
detail=r'''\subsection{Corrected Run Identities and Accounting}\label{app:ditl-evidence}
The authoritative registry binds all 24 files to SHA-256 identities. The corrected daily telemetry contains '''+f"{a['rows']} and {b['rows']} rows; annual telemetry contains {y['rows']} rows."+r''' All begin at elapsed zero and include the named endpoint. The annual span is exactly 365 days, from 2000-03-01 to 2001-03-01 UTC; the leap day precedes the start. This establishes timestamp coverage, not the missing runtime configuration or hardware validity. The former 50-day truncation finding applies only to superseded inputs.

No duplicate or nonmonotonic telemetry timestamps were found. Day-run timestamp differences are 2/20 s. Annual differences are 2/60 s with one 50 s interval, distinct from the current source default. Annual telemetry has 15161 mode changes versus 16283 transition records and 425 sampled Safe entries. Exact event checks are retained in the JSON audit. The expected adaptive schedule is unknown, so elapsed coverage alone cannot certify that every intended sample was exported. The last sample contributes no additional duration; its native increment fields remain included in cumulative data checks.
'''
detail+=table('Transition-log versus left-held telemetry mode duration (annual, seconds)','tab:annual-overlap',['Mode','Telemetry','Transitions'],[[tx(m),n(y['mode_seconds'].get(m,0)),n(y['event_mode_seconds'].get(m,0))] for m in sorted(set(y['mode_seconds'])|set(y['event_mode_seconds']))])
detail+=f"Transition mode sequence matches: {y['transition_mode_sequence_match']}; timestamp offset range is {tx(y['transition_offset_range_s']) if y['transition_offset_range_s'] is not None else 'undefined because the sequences differ'} (seconds where defined). Slew events total {n(y['event_checks']['slew_events']['sum_duration_s'])} s across {y['event_checks']['slew_events']['rows']} rows, distinct from {n(y['mode_seconds'].get('SLEWING',0))} s Slewing occupancy. These differences require the generating logger/control semantics, not fabricated interval adjustments.\n"
detail+=fig('day_modes','Corrected 24-hour mode timelines. Display-sampled points do not define the integration weights.','fig:corrected-day-modes')
detail+=fig('day_exposure_contacts','Exposure gates, eligible contact time and native transfer credits for the corrected day runs. Credits are not confirmed ground receipt.','fig:corrected-day-exposure')
detail+=fig('startup','Startup and Slewing duration from transition logs, shown separately from telemetry occupancy.','fig:corrected-startup')
detail+=r'''\subsection{Annual Exposure, Energy and Native Data}
'''
detail+=f"There are {y['event_checks']['saa_passes']['rows']} SAA event records and {y['sampled_saa_encounters']} sampled SAA windows. Independent science passages additionally require the approved eligibility and quality contract. The acquisition gate totals {n(y['acquisition_gate_s'])} s. Per-pass array sums and telemetry gate-array sums are {y['proton_pass_array_sum']:.6g} and {y['array_sum_on_gate']:.6g}; these are legacy model expectations, not reconstructed current-instrument events. Bin-wise rate-times-duration comparisons can differ after merging; effective channel metadata and dimensional calibration remain open.\n\n"
detail+=f"Recorded battery spans {y['battery_min_wh']:.6f}--{y['battery_max_wh']:.6f} Wh, ending at {y['final_battery_wh']:.6f} Wh. No negative battery row was found. The solar/load integrals are {y['generated_wh']:.3f}/{y['consumed_wh']:.3f} Wh under the stated interval convention. Charge efficiency, curtailment and post-step battery semantics prevent treating their difference as stored-energy margin or EOL feasibility.\n\n"
detail+=f"Native store begins at {n(y['initial_storage_source_mb'])}, peaks at {y['storage_max_source_mb']:.9f}, and ends at {n(y['final_storage_source_mb'])} source MB. Generation minus transfer closes against storage to {y['storage_balance_max_residual_source_mb']:.3g} source MB. Histogram-byte totals do not alone establish packet serialization completeness. Raw event packets, lost-event counters and ground-reception archives are absent.\n"
detail+=fig('annual_exposure_battery_contacts','Corrected 365-day exposure, battery envelope and contact availability; epoch 2000-03-01. These are recorded model predictions under unresolved runtime configuration.','fig:corrected-annual')
detail+=fig('annual_modes_cumulative','Annual telemetry mode occupancy and cumulative geographic versus acquisition-gate exposure. No mission-success classification is inferred.','fig:corrected-annual-modes')
detail+=fig('annual_native_data','Daily native generation/transfer and maximum source-labelled store. The historical native packet format is not Science Record v3.','fig:partial-storage')
write('detail',detail)
# v3 budget input
budget=table('Corrected annual sampled-gate workload, preferred three readings per visit','tab:tier-v3',['Tier','Gated visits','Records','Bytes','Peak queue'],[[t['tier'],n(t['science_enabled_visits']),n(t['records']),n(t['bytes']),n(next(v['peak_required_bytes'] for v in y['queues'] if v['case'].endswith(t['tier']+'_3')))] for t in y['tiers'] if t['readings']==3])
budget+=r'''These are hypothetical record slots on sample-owned geographic cells at 5, 1 and 0.5 degrees. Exact crossing times and actual readout boundaries are unavailable. Every gated interval is retained, including zero-count exposure; partitions are nonoverlapping. Interrupted acquisition imposes a fragmentation floor: more than three segments in a visit cannot be represented as three contiguous intervals without losing exposure or bridging shutdown. This interface conflict remains open; no duration/count threshold is invented. Multiple readings are not independent orbital passages.
'''
budget+=table('Corrected annual preferred EMSC queue outage sensitivity','tab:corrected-outage',['Removed service (days unless noted)','Peak bytes'],[[tx(v['outage_days']),n(v['worst_peak_bytes'])] for v in y['outages'] if v['case'].endswith('EMSC_3')])
budget+=f"Nominal EMSC peak is {n(q['peak_required_bytes'])} bytes, compared with 262144 bytes dedicated science RAM and 134217728 bytes candidate flash. These allocations must include queue metadata and other explicitly budgeted reserves; they are not total OBC memory. The 292-byte packed assembly plus illustrative 512-byte double histogram bank uses 804 bytes before stack, DMA, operating system and other subsystems. The corrected nominal queue {'exceeds' if q['peak_required_bytes']>262144 else 'fits within'} the candidate dedicated RAM before metadata. A 16 GB archive remains an optional retention trade, not a demonstrated minimum.\n\n"
budget+=f"The total-volume/eligible-time lower bound is {q['balance_lower_bound_bps']:.3f} bit/s for EMSC; it is not a guaranteed queue-closing bitrate because release timing and finite storage matter. Full-rate queue simulation transfers {n(q['transferred_bytes'])} bytes and leaves {n(q['remaining_bytes'])} bytes. Detailed ledgers retain each release, contact capacity, queue before/after, unused capacity and conserved byte balance. No physical link efficiency is inferred.\n"
budget+=fig('annual_v3_queue','Corrected annual v3 sensitivity, contact-end backlog. Within-contact and pre-contact peaks are given in the tables; this curve is not emitted telemetry.','fig:v3-queue')
budget+=f"For this release/service trace, binary search gives approximately {q.get('minimum_bitrate_final_balance_bps',0):.2f} bit/s to clear the final backlog (unbounded storage), versus the aggregate lower bound above. The 19200 bit/s reference is {q.get('rate_ratio_19200_to_final_balance',0):.2f} times this trace-specific value, not an RF margin. The longest no-service interval contains {q.get('generated_during_longest_gap_bytes',0)} generated bytes.\n"
write('budget',budget)
# GS table
write('contacts',table('Corrected source contacts and telemetry-Relay overlap at full ideal 19.2 kbps','tab:gs-v3-capacity',['Scenario','Contacts','Visible s','Relay s','Ideal Relay bytes'],[[tx(s),S[s]['contacts']['count'],n(S[s]['contacts']['duration_s']),n(S[s]['contacts']['relay_overlap_s']),n(S[s]['contacts']['relay_capacity_bytes'])] for s in SCENARIOS])+r'''The source station label is GS1\_India; BITS Goa is the planning station. Runtime station coordinates and elevation mask remain UNKNOWN. The producing mask is not applied again and no 10/15-degree conversion is attempted. All event timestamps identify 2000-03-01, not 2029. Native credit, ideal visibility capacity, ideal Relay capacity and future verified net throughput are distinct. Corrected per-contact and daily ledgers are in \path{data/derived/ditl_correction_2026-11-09/}.''')
# Audit documents, machine-readable metric migration.
changes=[]
for sc in SCENARIOS:
 old=json.loads((ROOT/'evidence/science-ditl/validation'/f'{sc}_summary.json').read_text());new=S[sc]
 mapping={'duration_s':'elapsed_s','saa_s':'saa_s','acquisition_gate_s':'acquisition_gate_s','battery_min_wh':'battery_min_wh','generated_wh':'generated_wh','consumed_wh':'consumed_wh','generated_source_mb':'generated_model_mb','transferred_source_mb':'transferred_model_mb','storage_max_source_mb':'storage_max_model_mb','contact_s':'contact_s'}
 for nk,ok in mapping.items():changes.append(dict(scenario=sc,metric=nk,superseded=old.get(ok),corrected=new[nk],change=new[nk]-old[ok] if ok in old else None,old_input='evidence/science_ditl/raw/'+sc+'_ANTARA_Science_telemetry.csv',old_result='evidence/science-ditl/validation/'+sc+'_summary.json',corrected_run=new['run_id'],new_result=str((OUT/(sc+'_summary.json')).relative_to(ROOT)),mcr_location='Sections 3–5; Appendices A.1/A.3/A.5/A.6/F'))
 for m in set(old['mode_seconds'])|set(new['mode_seconds']):changes.append(dict(scenario=sc,metric='mode_seconds:'+m,superseded=old['mode_seconds'].get(m,0),corrected=new['mode_seconds'].get(m,0),change=new['mode_seconds'].get(m,0)-old['mode_seconds'].get(m,0),old_input='evidence/science_ditl/raw/'+sc+'_ANTARA_Science_telemetry.csv',old_result='evidence/science-ditl/validation/'+sc+'_summary.json',corrected_run=new['run_id'],new_result=str((OUT/(sc+'_summary.json')).relative_to(ROOT)),mcr_location='Sections 4/F'))
dump(OUT/'claim_migration.json',changes)
base='Corrected source registry: `evidence/science-ditl/run_registry.json`. Recompute with `scripts/validate_corrected_ditl.py`; source hashes/headers are in `inventory.json`, numerical summaries and ledgers in `data/derived/ditl_correction_2026-11-09/`. Prior DITL conclusions are superseded, not silently retained.\n\n'
identity='| Run ID | Rows | Span (s) | Epoch | Verdict |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n'+'\n'.join(f"| `{s['run_id']}` | {s['rows']} | {s['duration_s']:g} | {s['epoch']} | {s['completeness']} |" for s in S.values())+'\n'
limits='''\nAll three runs have complete timestamp spans, but producing revision/configuration, RAAN, mass, integrator, runtime elevation mask and battery capacity remain UNKNOWN. Altitude is recorded directly; 25 Wh percentages are planning-normalized only. All event absolute/relative origins agree on 2000-03-01. A 365-day span ends 2001-03-01; February 29 precedes its start. No 2029 recalibration is claimed.\n\nNo duplicate or nonmonotonic telemetry timestamps or nonfinite selected scalar values were found. Observed adaptive cadences do not establish the expected sample schedule. Left-held telemetry intervals exclude final-row duration. Transition sequence and timestamp offsets are separately recorded; elapsed coverage is not proof of correct logger/control semantics. Comparison classification: SENSITIVITY ONLY (recorded orbit/contact similarity, runtime identity unverified).\n\nNative source-MB amounts are retained without silently choosing decimal versus binary scaling. Legacy model arrays and five-channel fields do not qualify current FPDU response. No accepted-event archive, reconstructed integer spectra, calibrated livetime, received packet archive or full hardware configuration is supplied. No MMSC/MSC/EMSC success metric is qualified by these outputs.\n'''
metrics='| Metric | LEOP 24h | No-LEOP 24h | LEOP 365d |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n'+'\n'.join('| '+title+' | '+' | '.join(n(val(s,k)) for s in [a,b,y])+' |' for title,k in rows)+'\n'
comparison='| Metric | LEOP | No LEOP | Difference (No−LEOP) | Percent vs LEOP |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'+'\n'.join(f"| {title} | {n(val(a,k))} | {n(val(b,k))} | {n(val(b,k)-val(a,k))} | {100*(val(b,k)-val(a,k))/val(a,k):.3f}% |" if val(a,k) else f"| {title} | 0 | {n(val(b,k))} | {n(val(b,k))} | undefined |" for title,k in rows)+'\n'
contact='| Run | Contacts | Contact s | Relay s | Ideal Relay bytes | Native transfer source MB |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'+'\n'.join(f"| {sc} | {s['contacts']['count']} | {n(s['contacts']['duration_s'])} | {n(s['contacts']['relay_overlap_s'])} | {n(s['contacts']['relay_capacity_bytes'])} | {s['transferred_source_mb']:.9f} |" for sc,s in S.items())+'\n'
queue='| Run/tier/readings | Generated bytes | Delivered bytes | Final bytes | Peak bytes |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'+'\n'.join(f"| {v['case']} | {v['generated_bytes']} | {v['transferred_bytes']} | {v['remaining_bytes']} | {v['peak_required_bytes']} |" for s in S.values() for v in s['queues'])+'\n'
outages='| Annual case | Outage | Worst peak bytes |\n|---|---|---:|\n'+'\n'.join(f"| {v['case']} | {v['outage_days']} | {v['worst_peak_bytes']} |" for v in y['outages'])+'\n'
validity='''\nRecord validity is separate from statistical precision and mission success. Zero-count exposures are retained. There is no arbitrary minimum reading duration. Ideal partitions conserve exposure and never bridge shutdown; real timing resolution remains unknown. If more than three acquisition fragments occur in a cell visit, preserving all contiguous intervals requires more than three records; this is flagged as an interface decision, not silently discarded exposure.\n\nQueue calculations use full 2400 bytes/s, initially empty v3 queues, no RF derating, and only source-contact/telemetry-Relay intersections. Native initial store is not silently counted as v3 science. Exact cell crossing times and hardware partition boundaries are absent, so these are time-aligned workload sensitivities, not demonstrated emitted records. All-particle electronics throughput is independent of this histogram byte budget.\n'''
reports={
'CORRECTED_DITL_RUN_VALIDATION':identity+limits+metrics,
'LEOP_VS_NO_LEOP_24H_VALIDATION':identity+comparison+limits+'\nBoth day runs have equal total acquisition gate; startup removal is not evidence of more qualified science. Event startup and Slewing are distinct from telemetry occupancy.\n',
'LEOP_1YR_CORRECTED_VALIDATION':identity+metrics+limits+contact+queue,
'SIMULATION_EVIDENCE_INGESTION':identity+limits+'\nIndependent radiation, geometric-factor, RAAN, thermal and dedicated detumble files were not replaced. Their preexisting limitations remain. Prior derived DITL outputs and PDFs are historical/superseded; original files are preserved.\n',
'SCIENCE_DITL_EVIDENCE_VALIDATION':identity+metrics+limits+validity,
'GS_PASS_CAPACITY_VALIDATION':contact+limits+'\nAOS/LOS subtraction and timestamp epoch checks are explicit. Apply no duplicate mask penalty. Telemetry and transition-log Relay overlap are separate calculations in each summary.\n',
'GS_19K2_LINK_CLOSURE':contact+queue+validity+'\n19.2 kbps is ideal gross capacity, not qualified application throughput. RF losses, packet overhead, coding and retransmissions are PDR closure. Minimum average balance rates alone do not guarantee finite-queue closure.\n',
'OBC_RAM_FLASH_SIZING':queue+outages+validity+'\nReference assembly:292 bytes. Illustrative double histogram bank:512 bytes. Working fixture:804 bytes before software/stack/DMA. Dedicated queue:256 KiB=262144 bytes (897 records before metadata). Candidate flash:128 MiB=134217728 bytes. Extended archive:16 GB usable, optional. Full OBC RAM is not defined by science-buffer allocation. Metadata, ECC, filesystem, housekeeping, power-loss recovery and retention reserve remain unallocated. The independent187498164-byte grid archive sensitivity still exceeds128MiB without delivery; it is not this annual gated run.\n',
'STORAGE_BACKLOG_VALIDATION':queue+outages+validity,
'TIER_RECORD_GENERATION':queue+validity+limits,
'INTEGRATED_SUBSYSTEM_CONSISTENCY':identity+limits+'\nCross-subsystem status: INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE for common runtime hardware/EPS/thermal identity. Dedicated thermal and detumble studies remain separate; no new combined margin is inferred.\n',
'DITL_CORRECTION_IMPACT_MATRIX':'| Scenario/metric | Superseded | Corrected | Change |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n'+'\n'.join(f"| {v['scenario']}/{v['metric']} | {n(v['superseded'])} | {n(v['corrected'])} | {n(v['change'])} |" for v in changes)+'\n\nThe complete machine-readable OLD INPUT → OLD RESULT → MCR LOCATION → CORRECTED RUN → NEW RESULT map is `claim_migration.json`; initial file/line references are in `initial_dependency_inventory.json`. Independent studies are unchanged unless explicitly cited as dependencies. Prior PDFs are immutable snapshots, not active authority.\n'}
for name,body in reports.items():(ROOT/'docs/audit'/f'{name}.md').write_text('# '+name.replace('_',' ')+' — corrected evidence 2026-11-09\n\n'+base+body)
